messages:
maya: FYI WellnessCo is stuck on onboarding because their mobile app's embedded webview is triggering a steady stream of 429s during SDK startup. They see this when users open the app, rotate the device, or switch accounts.

 devops-bot: alert -> unexpected-429-rate for customer=wellnessco key=sk_live_zzz window=2026-03-21T02:45Z peak=420r/s :warning:

 rene: Do we have their SDK init snippet and whether they're using background-sync or a service worker equivalent inside the webview?

 maya: Their engineers said they use the browser SDK inside a hybrid app webview and enabled the Background Sync API to queue offline writes. The SDK init is called on every visibilitychange event to ensure a token is fresh.

 omar: That's a strong smell. visibilitychange + background-sync replay = many concurrent handshake attempts. Also check whether their token mint endpoint returns unique ephemeral tokens per call (no reuse). If every tab/view gets a new ephemeral token, the handshake fanout explodes.

 kai: Reproduced quickly in a device lab: rotate -> visibilitychange fires twice -> SDK init called twice -> if network flaps the Background Sync replays queued request -> we get a 3x multiplier. Couple that with short-lived ephemeral tokens (TTL=20s) and you get a burst of handshake requests.

 rene: Edge layer behaviour note: we saw a lot of OPTIONS and POST /v1/sessions within 500ms windows. Cloud edge is rate-limiting per API key and treats ephemeral tokens the same as full keys for that metric. That makes client-side fanout particularly harmful during ramp.

 maya: Here's a sample failing request captured from their device (POST returns 429):

 -----
 POST /v1/sessions HTTP/1.1
 Host: api.redwood.example
 Authorization: Bearer eph_live_abc123
 Content-Type: application/json
 Content-Length: 128

 {"client_id":"wellness-mobile","platform":"android-webview","sdk_version":"web-1.9.2"}
 -----

 omar: Immediate mitigations we suggested to the customer: 1) debounce SDK.init on visibilitychange (e.g., 500ms) and guard against duplicate inits, 2) stop minting per-visibility token; instead mint on server and reuse token for a short window (recommended 5 minutes) across webview instances for a device, 3) disable Background Sync for the onboarding rollout while we monitor.

 kai: We also recommended handling 429s more gracefully in the SDK: respect Retry-After header, exponential backoff with jitter, and surface telemetry (a simple counter) so CS can see how often the SDK is hitting server-side throttles.

 maya: They did 1 & 2 quickly (debounce + server-issued ephemeral reuse) and toggled background sync off. Their rate dropped from ~420r/s to ~18r/s within ~7 minutes. They completed the onboarding flow afterwards.

 rene: Follow-ups: docs update for hybrid-webview gotcha + add a short KB snippet for renewals/customer-risk teams that flags "webview visibilitychange + background sync" as high-risk for scaling. Also we'll add an SDK safeguard to prevent concurrent init calls in the next patch.

 maya: I'll file a small PR for the handbook and schedule a 20-min runbook walk with WellnessCo engineers tomorrow. I'll also log this in Gainsight as onboarding risk mitigated and ping renewals.

 omar: Nice work — can we capture the debounce snippet for the KB? e.g.:

 -----
 let initTimeout = null;
 document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', () => {
   clearTimeout(initTimeout);
   initTimeout = setTimeout(() => {
     if (!sdk.isInitialized()) sdk.init();
   }, 500);
 });
 -----

 maya: Good call. Adding that to the KB. Closing the thread once PRs are up. :white_check_mark:
